  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10c-catfishes-remaining-catfish-from-south-america/trachydoras_paraguayensis_en/",
      "html": "<p>T. paraguayensis grows to around 10 cm long and can be kept in the same way as a larger species of Corydoras. This means: a peaceful fish, undemanding regarding food and likes to swim in company of its own kind.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/doradidae/trachydoras_paraguayensis.htm",
      "html": "<ul><li>Common name: Mouse Catfish</li><li>Synonym: Hemidoras paraguayensis</li><li>IUCN Red List: despite the little information available on this species, it has a wide range and no apparent threats. Therefore, it is assessed as Least Concern (IUCN 2024).</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10c-catfishes-remaining-catfish-from-south-america/trachydoras_paraguayensis_en/",
      "html": "<p>This charming species of thorny catfish comes from Paraguay.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/doradidae/trachydoras_paraguayensis.htm",
      "html": "<p>South America: Paraná River basin Paraguay, Brazil, Argentina, Bolivia. Type locality: Corumba, Brazil.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/doradidae/trachydoras_paraguayensis.htm",
      "html": "<p>From the Paraguay River at Corumba, Brazil.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "maintenance",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/doradidae/trachydoras_paraguayensis.htm",
      "html": "<p>Peaceful species for a mid sized community tank, planted with hiding places such as pipes or driftwood/bogwood.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/doradidae/trachydoras_paraguayensis.htm",
      "html": "<p>Tablet and pellet foods, frozen bloodworm and live foods should keep this catfish in good condition.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/doradidae/trachydoras_paraguayensis.htm",
      "html": "<p>Etymology: the specific name paraguayensis: –ensis, Latin suffix denoting place: Corumba, Paraguay, type locality.</p>"
    },
    {
